    "why": "decisions/0159 step 2 (Phase 6), part 1. Claude's finished build is a release zip merged into releases/inbox on degraffics/traversence's main. Every 10 minutes (the releases job), or at once with Releases ▾ → Check for builds in the site manager, the live site fetches each new zip through its GitHub key, checks its bytes against git's id, makes it a release and puts it straight onto staging, then takes it out of the inbox (git keeps its history). It shows in the site manager as on staging: look, then Publish. A zip is never made into a release twice. Uploading a zip still works.",
